es_out: with a subtitle track chosen, its decoder's first line before the start

When the buffering ends VLC waits for the video and sound decoders to have
their first data, not for the subtitle decoders: a subtitle decoder still
busy with the line at the start (looking for the video output, which the
video decoder makes only then) handed its line over after the first picture
was shown. With a subtitle track chosen at the start (sub-track-id) and a
video, VLC also waits for the subtitle decoders that are busy with a block;
an idle one with nothing to decode doesn't hold the start (input_DecoderWait
stops waiting on a decoder that is idle with an empty queue). Applied after
0002, with patch -p1 (Scripts/build_vlckit_lgpl.sh).

diff --git a/src/input/es_out.c b/src/input/es_out.c
--- a/src/input/es_out.c
+++ b/src/input/es_out.c
@@ -710,15 +710,32 @@
     }
 
     const vlc_tick_t i_decoder_buffering_start = mdate();
+    /* Changed for Schnellbild on 2026-11-15: Scripts/vlc-patches/0003-es_out-with-a-subtitle-track-chosen-its-first-line-before-the-start.patch */
+    bool b_video = false;
     for( int i = 0; i < p_sys->i_es; i++ )
     {
         es_out_id_t *p_es = p_sys->es[i];
 
         if( !p_es->p_dec || p_es->fmt.i_cat == SPU_ES )
             continue;
+        if( p_es->fmt.i_cat == VIDEO_ES )
+            b_video = true;
         input_DecoderWait( p_es->p_dec );
         if( p_es->p_dec_record )
             input_DecoderWait( p_es->p_dec_record );
+    }
+    /* A subtitle track chosen at the start (sub-track-id) with a video: its
+     * decoder, busy with a block it was given, finishes it first, so the
+     * line it holds reaches the first picture (an idle one with nothing to
+     * decode doesn't hold the start) */
+    if( b_video && var_GetInteger( p_sys->p_input, "sub-track-id" ) >= 0 )
+    {
+        for( int i = 0; i < p_sys->i_es; i++ )
+        {
+            es_out_id_t *p_es = p_sys->es[i];
+            if( p_es->p_dec && p_es->fmt.i_cat == SPU_ES )
+                input_DecoderWait( p_es->p_dec );
+        }
     }
 
     msg_Dbg( p_sys->p_input, "Decoder wait done in %d ms",
